  "open_questions": [
    "SSI discrepancy, not reconciled: Afton's HiTEC 5748 PDS prints 'Shear Stability Index %: 22' (05/23 and 04/21) and 'a typical Shear Stability Index (SSI) of 22' (03/18); the 07/11 edition says 'It is based on 23 SSI polymer' (base-polymer basis); Afton's HiTEC 12360 bulletin DL2-13692.pdf (07/20, p.2) describes 'HiTEC® 5748 25SSI OCP' / '25SSI viscosity modifier'. None of these documents prints the SSI test method, cycle count or base oil, so comparability is not established and no conflict entry is recorded. Confirm the SSI and its method with Afton.",
    "Treat range: the PDS gives one dosage per SAE grade in vol.% for the 10 hour L-38 stay-in-grade requirement, with CMCC (DIN 51382) values in parentheses (kept as alternate_entries); no min/max range and no wt.% basis are printed.",
    "Thickening response, post-shear KV100, HTHS, CCS/MRV impact, low-temperature gelation, active polymer content, carrier and dissolution/blend temperature are not printed; left Missing. The printed 'Dilute Viscosity @ 100°C, cSt: 11.55' has no stated reference oil or dose, so it is not entered as a thickening response."
  ],
